  {
   "id": 614997,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure><img src=\"exercises/media/0585a919b75f22fb.png\" alt=\"An engraving titled “The Federal pillars.” Five pillars are labeled from left to right “Del.”, “Pen.”, “N. Jer.”, “Geor.”, and “Con.”. A sixth pillar, burning and falling to the right, is labeled “Mass.”. Under the pillars text reads “United they stand—divided fall”.\">\n<figcaption>The Federal Pillars.</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "\n<p><i>Refer to the image provided.</i></p>\nThe image shown best supports which argument of the ratification debate?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167958,
     "content_html": "The need for a bill of rights to curtail the powers of the central government and guarantee people’s individual liberties"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167959,
     "content_html": "The potential destruction of deliberation and creation of rival factions"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167960,
     "content_html": "The view that states need to stand individually without an overarching, omnipotent central government"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167961,
     "content_html": "The need for states to support and ratify the Constitution to guarantee the existence of a republican union"
    }
   ],
